 after Republican Tommy Tuberville retired to run for governor, but the race remains firmly in Republican hands. Congressman Barry Moore won the GOP nomination with Trump's backing and heads into the general election with a massive resource edge: roughly $3.8 million raised and $16.5 million in outside support, plus a Trump rally planned in Mobile. Democrat Everett Wess has raised about $81,000 and faces long odds in a state with a 15-point Republican lean.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the contest Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets price Moore's chances near 98 percent. The only available poll, from July, showed Moore ahead by 15 points. A bribery accusation tied to Moore's support for a Trump election offer has drawn headlines, but nothing suggests it threatens the seat. The forecast expects a Republican win by roughly 18 points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -14.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.004, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.018, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0262, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0053, "margin": -18.0}]}